lease that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so it was not used.) After the rollback, the service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15657, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01N2ee7o29pv7UVi4wzuJzUt", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15657, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01N2ee7o29pv7UVi4wzuJzUt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18829, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** I went back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. I skipped v2.3.1-rc because it had only been healthy in staging, not production.\n- **Check afterward:** all three regions are running v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before v2.3.1 is deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JD5iCd3hjcwgbeHGkAxDCG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NuMLrA13w7exp4iRbYpzRC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "